  <uml:Package xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499781275503_964108_36116" xmi:uuid="07d8eda6-d167-4328-8325-e7d78e6c1bad" xmi:type="uml:Package">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_45e01bd_1513335976478_297974_79647" xmi:uuid="0cb4a8ed-fce9-4eb3-b3c5-cbf318ea4650" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
      <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499781275503_964108_36116"/>
      <body>This capability enables the representation of a kinematic mechanism and specific states of it in two alternative ways.&lt;br&gt; In the first alternative, the motion of objects are not constrained by each other and each object follows its own path in space. &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;The paths of all objects are controlled and coordinated by a common time parameter.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; In the second alternative, the motion of objects are constrained with each other by kinematic pairs that hold information about the type of kinematic joint. &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;An overall kinematic state of such a mechanism is defined by the state of each kinematic pair. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Motion is defined by a sequence of kinematic states controlled by a time parameter.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The Figure &lt;caption&gt;Simplified overview of the AP242 kinematics Domain model&lt;/caption&gt; provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;Kinematics_domainModel_Overview.png&lt;/name&gt;Simplified overview of the AP242 kinematics Domain model&lt;/figure&gt; These concepts are used in this capability: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;the yaw represents the angle by which the original frame (x0; y0; z0) is rotated first about the z-axis to yield an intermediate (x′, y′, z′) frame;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;the pitch represents the angle by which the intermediate frame (x′, y′, z′) then is rotated about the y′-axis to yield another intermediate (x″, y″, z″) frame;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;the roll represents the angle by which the (x″, y″, z″) frame is rotated about the x″-axis to yield the desired final (x, y, z) frame.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; Figure &lt;caption&gt;Description of yaw, pitch, and roll angles&lt;/caption&gt; describes these concepts in the case of a LowOrderKinematicPair where (x1, y1, z1) is the first pair frame, and (x2, y2, z2) is the second pair frame. (x', y', z') is an intermediate frame resulting from the yaw rotation of (x1, y1, z1) about z1. (x", y", z") results from the pitch rotation of (x', y', z') about y'. The roll rotation of (x", y", z") about x" produces (x2, y2, z2). &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;yaw_pitch_roll.gif&lt;/name&gt;Description of yaw, pitch, and roll angles&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;note&gt;For more detailed information on yaw, pitch, and roll convention see ISO 8855&lt;/note&gt;</body>
    </ownedComment>
    <name>Kinematics</name>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702983794419_578513_66450" xmi:uuid="00ad396a-5f5d-4055-ba30-6d4829a0f6ef" xmi:type="uml:Association">
