    <packagedElement xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618559_111063_66555" xmi:uuid="57b1b06e-a3e2-46e4-a28f-f93ac9c1dcc7" xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618561_825565_66560" xmi:uuid="1cc63df4-e0e3-4cc1-8c50-c1e743f53ce0" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618559_111063_66555"/>
        <body>A KinematicPairWithMotionCouplingTypeEnum type lists the possible types of a KinematicPairWithMotionCoupling.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>KinematicPairWithMotionCouplingTypeEnum</name>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618560_364724_66556" xmi:uuid="5e25bc54-935c-4c32-b126-54a03e44d38b" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618561_742103_66562" xmi:uuid="bc31d21c-d388-4918-8c9d-342c06b10042" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618560_364724_66556"/>
          <body> a pair made of two revolute pairs coupled via Radius or via CouplingRatio.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>gear_pair</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618560_152256_66557" xmi:uuid="e16ee41d-bfcb-4b50-b5cd-14a55257f7c4" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618561_45186_66563" xmi:uuid="b85ef8d9-3c24-4b8d-b991-015b08c6f7f6" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618560_152256_66557"/>
          <body> a pair that consists of a linear flexible link that moves around a rolling (virtual) pinion where the rotation axis of the pinion is perpendicular to the direction of the linear flexible link. A pair made of two prismatic pairs coupled via Radius or via CouplingRatio.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>linear_flexible_and_pinion_pair</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618560_318506_66558" xmi:uuid="215e42c5-854c-4f20-982d-f74cc04914f0" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618561_403996_66564" xmi:uuid="59000b09-dca2-43df-bffa-d9ee036b69ba" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984618560_318506_66558"/>
          <body> a pair that describes a pinion rolling on a rack where the rotation axis of the pinion is perpendicular to the direction of the rack. A pair made of one revolute and one prismatic pair coupled via Radius or via CouplingRatio.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>rack_and_pinion_pair</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984706598_742358_66570" xmi:uuid="65111d0b-901d-4f92-8a85-93b7140085d1" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1704730232120_102695_60180" xmi:uuid="c938a499-4fde-49d4-9ddc-f10b0d03ff0d" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984706598_742358_66570"/>
          <body>a pair made of two universal pairs where the rotation of input axis and output axis are uniform. The Rotation axis of Pairs[1].Link1 and Pairs[2].Link2 shall be parallel. Pairs[1].Link2 and Pairs[2].Link1 shall reference either the same Occurrence of a Part, or both Occurrences shall be joined via a fully_constrained_pair. In the latter case, three Pairs are involved: universal_pair, fully_constrained_pair and universal_pair. </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>composed_homokinetic_pair</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984805938_667170_66571" xmi:uuid="7976fdf4-de0b-49aa-9810-827800db6f0e" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1704730387841_208371_60187" xmi:uuid="5cec4efd-da48-43bf-bf23-c054c0ed53d9" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984805938_667170_66571"/>
          <body>a pair made of one revolute_pair, prismatic_pair, or cylindrical_pair driving the motion of one other revolute_pair, prismatic_pair, or cylindrical_pair coupled via a Radius or via a CouplingRatio. &lt;note&gt; gear_pair and rack_and_pinion_pair are simple cases of this kind of pair. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>two_joint_coupler</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
      <ownedLiteral xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984843449_14573_66572" xmi:uuid="3364180b-cced-41ee-bacc-7082deee8d74" xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1704730434278_79574_60192" xmi:uuid="9fbeeadd-89a4-4c3f-9c40-e9a1fa0488f3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702984843449_14573_66572"/>
          <body>a pair made of one revolute_pair, prismatic_pair, or cylindrical_pair driving the motion of two other revolute_pairs, prismatic_pairs, and/or cylindrical_pairs coupled via two Radius or via two CouplingRatios</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>three_joint_coupler</name>
      </ownedLiteral>
    </packagedElement>
