    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193199_696611_23775" xmi:uuid="80b94551-4d08-45b4-a6d2-42ca796af2df" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1513352098640_726647_86554" xmi:uuid="d7388376-f596-4e6e-821b-21cc0fc85a7a" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193199_696611_23775"/>
        <body>A ProductStructureKinematicPathAssociation is an association of one KinematicsPathDefinedByNodes within the items of a LinkMotionAlongPath and one Occurrence within an AssemblyDefinition. &lt;note&gt;A ProductStructureKinematicsPathAssociation can be used instead of a combination of LinkMotionTransformation, LinkMotionRelationship and ProductStructureLinkMotionAssociation for the case that the underlying PartView has only one geometric Model associated to it and that LinkMotionTransformation.TransformItem1 is equal to an AxisPlacement with no translation and no rotation.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ProductStructureKinematicPathAssociation</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551459818804_988250_180348" xmi:uuid="3dc48549-34f7-4f44-ad68-e33093c348b1" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551459893314_424641_180358" xmi:uuid="820d7380-b60f-4872-9799-bad8ae1d80c4" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551459818804_988250_180348"/>
          <body>the attribute SubStructure that points to a SpecifiedOccurrence, shall belong with their attributes UpperUsage in a recursive way to an Occurrence that is called out by the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ProductDataManagement.htm#ViewOccurrenceRelationship.Related&lt;/path&gt; Related&lt;/a&gt; attribute belonging to the AssociatedTo.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721730195326_258533_153287" xmi:uuid="96ce0bee-7821-46c1-be52-b378e6c723d0" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721730195326_407049_153288" xmi:uuid="0c5da510-48ae-4702-994b-b5702fba77ce" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body> &lt;sch:rule context="//ProductStructureKinematicPathAssociation[@uid]"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="entity_name" value="if(@xsi:type) then substring-after(@xsi:type,':') else name()"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="associatedTo_Related_uidRef" value="../Related/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="upperUsage" value="local-fn:MainUpperUsage(//DataContainer, Substructure/@uidRef)"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="$associatedTo_Related_uidRef = $upperUsage"&gt; The attribute SubStructure that points to a SpecifiedOccurrence, shall belong with their attributes UpperUsage in a recursive way to an Occurrence that is called out by the Related attribute belonging to the AssociatedTo. { -entity_name:&lt;sch:value-of select="$entity_name"/&gt; -entity_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt; -rule_name:WR2 } &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR2</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193199_696611_23775"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551459818804_194881_180349" xmi:uuid="640107df-8fc3-4ec7-be35-21a66a4bb2f4" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>self.Substructure-&gt;closure(UpperUsage)-&gt;select(e | e.UpperUSage.oclIsUndefined()) = self.AssociatedTo.Related</body>
          <language>OCL2.0</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551459804297_871094_180346" xmi:uuid="dd54bcdd-884e-4126-8fe7-f5c5d1aae101" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721730195316_417437_153285" xmi:uuid="131a11f7-d7b7-48be-aa1d-ad59b5f0552a" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721730195316_60305_153286" xmi:uuid="fb69a687-15d4-4eec-bbe0-97c1316d6143" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body> &lt;sch:rule context="//ProductStructureKinematicPathAssociation[@uid]"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="entity_name" value="if(@xsi:type) then substring-after(@xsi:type,':') else name()"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="assembly_definition_by_associatedTo_relating_uid" value="../../@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="link_motion_along_path_uid" value="AssociatedMotionRepresentation/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="motion_model_association_uid" value="//*/MotionModelAssociation/AssociatedModel[@uidRef = $link_motion_along_path_uid]/../@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="assembly_definition_by_associated_motion_representation_uid" value="//*/MotionModelAssociation/AssociatedModel[@uidRef = $link_motion_along_path_uid]/../../@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="$assembly_definition_by_associatedTo_relating_uid = $assembly_definition_by_associated_motion_representation_uid"&gt; The AssemblyDefinition called out by the AssociatedTo attribute of the MotionModelAssociation linked to the AssociatedMotionRepresentation attribute of type LinkMotionAlongPath shall be the same as the one pointed by the Relating attribute of the AssociatedTo. { -entity_name:&lt;sch:value-of select="$entity_name"/&gt; -entity_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt; -rule_name:WR1 -assembly_definition_by_associatedTo_relating_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$assembly_definition_by_associatedTo_relating_uid"/&gt; -link_motion_along_path_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$link_motion_along_path_uid"/&gt; -motion_model_association_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$motion_model_association_uid"/&gt; -assembly_definition_by_associated_motion_representation_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$assembly_definition_by_associated_motion_representation_uid"/&gt; } &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551711106257_306172_182241" xmi:uuid="ddc6e113-09b6-4e2e-b494-49984680b68c" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551459804297_871094_180346"/>
          <body>the AssemblyDefinition called out by the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_Kinematics.htm#MotionModelAssociation.AssociatedTo&lt;/path&gt; AssociatedTo&lt;/a&gt; attribute of the MotionModelAssociation linked to the AssociatedMotionRepresentation attribute of type LinkMotionAlongPath shall be the same as the one pointed by the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ProductDataManagement.htm#AssemblyOccurrenceRelationship.Relating&lt;/path&gt; Relating&lt;/a&gt; attribute of the AssociatedTo.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR1</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193199_696611_23775"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551459804299_700523_180347" xmi:uuid="da225522-7f7b-4691-8ac2-2ce34e03c73d" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>self.AssociatedTo.Relating = self.AssociatedMotionRepresentation.motionModelAssociation.AssociatedTo</body>
          <language>OCL2.0</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721221107080_458324_148782" xmi:uuid="07f383d3-84c4-4ad4-9acb-78e53b1d7a77" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
