    <packagedElement xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028" xmi:uuid="a5ce3bc5-4fbb-402d-80ae-39afc87ff826" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1705417074097_291497_159889" xmi:uuid="2550479f-f52c-49ae-815d-84494734cd9e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <body>No mapping: ARM/MIM concept will be developed when more review and experience on the new feature by the Kinematics implementors at the PDM-IF first will be available.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920947_796091_64084" xmi:uuid="7b94a957-4ffa-46ee-94a3-bcd8c8c4a050" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028"/>
        <body>A KinematicPairWithMotionCoupling is a type of RepresentationItem that specifies a motion constraint defined by one or more KinematicPairs.&lt;note&gt;Having too few drivers (under-definition) or too many drivers (over-definition) in a 'two_joint_coupler' or a 'three_joint_coupler' is tolerated, but the coupler will not run.&lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt;For 'two_joint_coupler' or 'three_joint_coupler', the kinematic solver of the CAD system computes the displacement of each joint having a driver and derives the displacement of the remaining joint that has no driver according to the following coupling formula that involves all the displacements 'd' and all the scales 's':&lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;s1.d1 + s2.d2 = 0 (for a two_joint_coupler)&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;s1.d1 + s2.d2 + s3.d3 = 0 (for a three_joint_coupler).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt;For 'two_joint_coupler' and 'three_joint_coupler', there is no restriction about the parts involved as Link1 / Link2 of one pair to their re-use or not in the other coupled pair(s).&lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt;The Link1 of each combined pair may be the BaseLink of the Mechanism or different. A part used as Link1 (fixed part) in one pair may be used as Link2 (moving part) of the other coupled pair(s). So a 'two_joint_coupler' may involve 2 to 4 links and a three_joint_coupler 3 to 6 links.&lt;/example&gt;&lt;example&gt;The Figure &lt;caption&gt;Joint Coupler&lt;/caption&gt; shows a simple example with 4 KinematicLinks, 3 joints, 2 drivers for a 3-joint coupler.&lt;/example&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;JointCoupler.gif&lt;/name&gt;Joint Coupler&lt;/figure&gt; </body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>KinematicPairWithMotionCoupling</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723209315570_868062_60630" xmi:uuid="0052e9ba-4b84-46f1-91fe-553980350dc2" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723209396974_896208_60632" xmi:uuid="3ec9f758-a7a0-46d6-98e8-b09623eb6c08" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1723209315570_868062_60630"/>
          <body>Scales shall be either undefined or its size shall be greater or equal 2.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR1</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723209315581_941146_60631" xmi:uuid="cd3a225f-c0d7-421f-b2fb-51f3e10bc16d" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>self.Scales-&gt;isEmpty() xor (Scales-&gt;size() &gt;= 2)</body>
          <language>English</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210788551_199564_60698" xmi:uuid="0dbc389f-cabf-49a1-a9dd-a339d5db7a41" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210804501_954110_60700" xmi:uuid="9e1cc913-9c9d-43e6-8759-cd572665b0d6" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210788551_199564_60698"/>
          <body>for 'gear_pair', 'linear_flexible_and_pinion_pair' and 'gear_pair', Link1 of both coupled pairs may be the BaseLink of the Mechanism or the same non-BaseLink part or different, but both Link2 have to be different.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>IP16</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210788555_724011_60699" xmi:uuid="269723cf-4ecb-45fb-bcb0-ecef97990b6b" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>For 'gear_pair', 'linear_flexible_and_pinion_pair' and 'gear_pair', Link1 of both coupled pairs may be the BaseLink of the Mechanism or the same non-BaseLink part or different, but both Link2 have to be different.</body>
          <language>English</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723209941605_541310_60637" xmi:uuid="31fc7f6e-8fa9-4f79-93f4-583f47eabfa7" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723209986942_266737_60639" xmi:uuid="e81ba2a6-0b26-4e77-8851-718bfb9632bd" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1723209941605_541310_60637"/>
          <body>CouplingTypes shall be either undefined or its size shall be greater or equal 2.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR2</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723209941612_152645_60638" xmi:uuid="3fac1165-4dfe-491e-9a64-7cf45d078a26" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>self.CouplingTypes-&gt;isEmpty() xor (CouplingTypes-&gt;size() &gt;= 2)</body>
          <language>English</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210543561_105952_60677" xmi:uuid="3577d360-b05c-470b-a4cf-5e3c027afeff" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210556296_792153_60679" xmi:uuid="41fcf4ce-e2b2-4373-9598-13f36d6511fb" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210543561_105952_60677"/>
          <body>if the Z axles have opposite directions, the related Scale shall have a negative value.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>IP9</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210543566_667672_60678" xmi:uuid="ec55dd88-b2e1-4e2f-8887-774b30fbb5a5" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>If the Z axles have opposite directions, the related Scale shall have a negative value.</body>
          <language>English</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210285577_902213_60659" xmi:uuid="5986ccb2-ad9d-4b6a-9131-e08c3fd7929d" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210355740_365683_60661" xmi:uuid="925d435a-c697-47e5-b044-8f589fd10efd" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210285577_902213_60659"/>
          <body>the value of Scales[n] shall apply to the pair mapped to Pairs[n].</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>IP3</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210285581_470487_60660" xmi:uuid="5140bc06-4094-47dc-b797-ce87a5043b69" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>The value of Scales[n] shall apply to the pair mapped to Pairs[n].</body>
          <language>English</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210676091_444801_60689" xmi:uuid="59e9d61d-95cc-42b6-b557-06a03a328e07" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210696183_986534_60691" xmi:uuid="ededd542-d1a4-4c05-95e1-fcce27725c74" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210676091_444801_60689"/>
          <body>for 'gear_pair', either CouplingRatios[1] or Radius[1] and Radius[2] should be mapped, since both values are related to each other: the conversion formula between both is: CouplingRatio = Radius1/Radius2.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>IP13</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210676099_507889_60690" xmi:uuid="def78f0b-fb4c-4459-b499-d1d1cb4e8ba3" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>For 'gear_pair', either CouplingRatios[1] or Radius[1] and Radius[2] should be mapped, since both values are related to each other: the conversion formula between both is: CouplingRatio = Radius1/Radius2.</body>
          <language>English</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210598644_737945_60683" xmi:uuid="5c2c7ead-edc2-4724-ae09-3f1e5881599b" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210614272_183654_60685" xmi:uuid="4c43fcd3-4a4f-4904-8bc9-e1bb643ad9b5" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210598644_737945_60683"/>
          <body>for 'rack_and_pinion_pair', either CouplingRatios[1] or Radius[1] should be mapped, since both values are related to each other: the conversion formula between both is: CouplingRatio = 2 * PI * Radius.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>IP11</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702978920923_682940_64028"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210598647_218852_60684" xmi:uuid="e9151d44-7c9b-4284-8881-a01ef306fb99" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>For 'rack_and_pinion_pair', either CouplingRatios[1] or Radius[1] should be mapped, since both values are related to each other: the conversion formula between both is: CouplingRatio = 2 * PI * Radius.</body>
          <language>English</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_2840147_1723210408763_795494_60665" xmi:uuid="63c64278-662e-4fec-b03c-8429fb534de5" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
