        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193186_665022_23751"/>
        <body>A PointToPointPath is a type of PathSegment definition of a kinematic path by means of frames that shall be traversed. It does not include a prescribed interpolation. &lt;note&gt; The interpolation is left to the software that uses the data. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; A PointToPointPath describes a discontinuous motion, which is indicated by the inherited attribute transition with the value 'discontinuous'.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>PointToPointPath</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193892_339428_28132" xmi:uuid="5098869a-8e78-4865-b954-7200891274db" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
